plan-audit.md:355:**Fix.** Refine the rule into three tiers and publish it in the README isolation contract. (1) BANNED on every day, no exceptions: any `wp action-scheduler run` without a specific action id, and any `--hooks=` drain. (2) PERMITTED on any day: running ONE action by id from Tools -> Scheduled Actions, and queueing a single-subscription action and letting the per-minute cron claim it - provided the task first screenshots the Pending queue for the next 60 minutes and aborts if any non-SLT action is due. (3) D8 ONLY: editing _next_payment_date / _end_date / _renewal_scheduled_date to move an event in time, always paired with the 13 non-SLT _next_payment_date before/after proof. Under this rule LIFE-04 step 9, EML-01 step 8, EML-10 and ADM-05/03 are legal where they are; LIFE-01 and SETUP-99 stay on D8/D10 with the pre-flight. For SETUP-99, replace 'search and cancel' with 'cancel by action id, taken from the per-subscription action-id metas recorded in the registry'. For SLT-ADM-01, keep the bulk dialog cancelled and file the missing-guard finding as a bug, as authored.
